# Source Bridge core

User-to-user sourcing marketplace. UI language: Protected Payment / Direct Payment — never “escrow”.

## Roles (never collapse)

- **Proposer** (`createdById`): submitted the current Payment Ticket revision; auto-approves it.
- **Buyer** (`buyerId`): pays; only buyer may start funding.
- **Sourcer** (`sellerId`): seller entitlement and Stripe Connect destination.

Creating a ticket does not make the creator the buyer. Any two eligible users use the same architecture.

## Account independence

CORE MARKETPLACE FUNCTIONALITY MUST BE ACCOUNT-INDEPENDENT. No feature is complete if it only works for historical test accounts. Critical flows use generic-user fixtures. Canonical identity is `User.id`.

Do not hardcode `futureman`, `theowlsaid`, their emails/IDs, conversation IDs, or transaction IDs except when a QA task names a historical fixture. Core tests use generic User A/B/C/D.

## Money

Integer minor units. Server calculation is authoritative; UI estimates are not. Historical funded records keep the fee stored at creation — never retroactively rewrite them.

## This repo

Next.js App Router, Prisma, Stripe LIVE (`LIVE_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=true`). Payment architecture is **PRODUCTION-FROZEN**. Do not change product behaviour in tooling/docs tasks.
